{"name":"Tidal Basin","hex":"#78b3cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tidal basin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of basin, usually provided for shipping, where the tide rises and falls, without a constant depth of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tidal_basin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tidal Basin","blocks":[{"text":"The Tidal Basin is a man-made reservoir located between the Potomac River and the Washington Channel in Washington, D.C. The Basin is part of West Potomac Park, is near the National Mall and is a focal point of the National Cherry Blossom Festival held each spring. The nearby Jefferson Memorial, Martin Luther King Jr. Memorial and Franklin Delano Roosevelt Memorial overlook the Basin, which is south of the Washington Monument."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Tidal_Basin_Glow.jpg/330px-Tidal_Basin_Glow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tidal_Basin","wikidata":"Q956781"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/West_potomac_park.jpg/330px-West_potomac_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e6/West_potomac_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/West_potomac_park.jpg/330px-West_potomac_park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWest_potomac_park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Tidal_Basin_photographers_and_painter.jpg/500px-Tidal_Basin_photographers_and_painter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Tidal_Basin_photo